  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that switching the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 in the multimodal/multiprofile/avgpool/weighted setting (config_031 vs config_019) yielded a substantial +3.9 pp accuracy gain (0.678 vs 0.639), making the RNA encoder the most impactful design axis. However, we have only tested one learned encoder (scvi_n200) and cannot yet tell whether this gain is specific to scvi or a general property of learned RNA encoders. config_043 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is a clean A/B comparison against config_031 on the single variable of RNA encoder. It will clarify whether scgpt matches or exceeds scvi_n200, or whether scvi_n200 is uniquely suited to this task. Under a limited budget, resolving the most influential design decision (RNA encoder choice) before further exploring the image-encoder or aggregation dimensions is the highest-information next step: if scgpt is competitive, it opens an additional viable path; if it underperforms, we confirm scvi_n200 as the preferred encoder and can commit remaining budget to refining the image-encoder and fusion choices around it."
}

